Subject: [PATCH] vayu_wifi W25j: a fresh 802.11 sequence number for every data frame (the 4/4 was
 being dropped as a duplicate), and the diagnostics that show it

Base: /mnt/ramdisk/ds-wifi2 as run 132300 (kernel mach-wifi25i).  W25i got the whole 4-way through
-- 1/4 -> 2/4, 3/4 verified, 4/4 sent, keys installed, en0 up -- yet DHCP never got a lease and
the AP deauthenticated us 3.3 s after its 3/4 with reason 15 (4WAY_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT).

What the 132300 log says, byte by byte:
 - our 4/4 is well formed: 08 01 | bssid | us | bssid | seq 00 00 | aa aa 03 00 00 00 88 8e |
   01 03 00 5f | desc 2 | key_info 0x030a | replay 2 | nonce 0 | key data 0, and its TX
   completion was status 0 (sent and ACKed).
 - but every data frame we built carried sequence control 00 00: the 2/4, the 4/4, and all six
   DHCP DISCOVERs (and everything iOS sent) -- we never assigned a sequence number, mac80211 does
   that in Linux and nothing does it here.
 - the AP takes the first data frame with a sequence number (the 2/4), and its duplicate cache
   then drops the next one from the same address and TID with the same number: the 4/4.  It
   retransmits 3/4 (we are already KEYED and ignored it), the 4-way timer expires: DEAUTH reason
   15.  From then on the port is closed, every data frame goes unacknowledged, which is the
   firmware's HTT TX status 5 the log shows four times (the first DISCOVER was already sent after
   the 4/4, inside the duplicate window).

Changes:
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_scan.c, vayu_scan_tx_frame(): the frame is written to the HTT TX pool and
   gets seq = ++tx_seq & 0xfff in its sequence control field (bytes 22-23, seq << 4); the 50-byte
   prefetch is copied from the pool copy, so the head the firmware reads has the same number.
   One counter for all data: everything we send is non-QoS (the assoc request has no WMM IE).
 - diagnostics, no secrets: first 8 data TX (length, clear/encrypted, multicast, seq), first 16
   data RX (length, decap, attention, DECRYPT_ERR bit 29, MPDU encrypted bit 13, encrypt type,
   Protected bit, MPDU_END decrypt error, ethertype, UDP ports), a completion status histogram
   (0..7) in vayu_scan_tx_summary() called from vayu_net_summary(), every DHCP frame to port 68
   with its xid, EAPOL arriving after the keys (the AP retransmitting 3/4 = it did not take the
   4/4), and the raw four words of VDEV_INSTALL_KEY_COMPLETE (0x5003, tag 0x2a).

Expected on the next run: txdata #0..#3 with seq 1,2,3,4 (not 0), no "eapol after the keys",
no DEAUTH reason 15, TX status histogram all 0, and then "W25 S5 dhcp: OK offer ..." and
"OK bound ..." followed by the ARP/ICMP probe lines.

Artifact: /mnt/ramdisk/ds-wifi-out/mach-wifi25j.bin 16461280 B
